{"type":"DocumentElement","title":"01: AsciiDoc delimiter mappings hardcoded in CoreModel","children":[{"type":"SectionElement","title":"01: AsciiDoc delimiter mappings hardcoded in CoreModel","level":1,"children":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"Status: FIXED","level":2,"children":[]},{"type":"ListBlock","marker_type":"unordered","items":[{"type":"ListItem","children":[{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"DELIMITER_CHAR_TO_SEMANTIC"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" constant removed from "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"CoreModel::Block"}],"marker":"*","content":"`DELIMITER_CHAR_TO_SEMANTIC` constant removed from `CoreModel::Block`"},{"type":"ListItem","children":[{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"delimiter_to_semantic_type"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" method removed from "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"BlockBuilder"}],"marker":"*","content":"`delimiter_to_semantic_type` method removed from `BlockBuilder`"},{"type":"ListItem","children":[{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"delimiter_type"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" attribute retained on "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"Block"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" for format-specific round-trip serialization (correct design)"}],"marker":"*","content":"`delimiter_type` attribute retained on `Block` for format-specific round-trip serialization (correct design)"}]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"BoldElement","children":[],"content":"Severity:"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" CRITICAL  "},{"type":"TextContent","text":"\n"},{"type":"BoldElement","children":[],"content":"Location:"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb"},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"lib/ceradoc/core_model/builder/block_builder.rb"}],"content":"**Severity:** CRITICAL  \n**Location:** `lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb`, `lib/ceradoc/core_model/builder/block_builder.rb`","callouts":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"Problem","level":2,"children":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"TextContent","text":"CoreModel is the format-neutral hub, yet it contains hardcoded AsciiDoc delimiter-to-semantics mappings in TWO places. The characters "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"-"},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"="},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"_"},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"*"},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"."},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"+"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" and the convention of 4-character delimiters are AsciiDoc-specific. Markdown uses fences (```), HTML uses tags ("},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"<pre>"},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"<blockquote>"},{"type":"TextContent","text":"). This knowledge has no place in the core."}],"content":"CoreModel is the format-neutral hub, yet it contains hardcoded AsciiDoc delimiter-to-semantics mappings in TWO places. The characters `-`, `=`, `_`, `*`, `.`, `+` and the convention of 4-character delimiters are AsciiDoc-specific. Markdown uses fences (```), HTML uses tags (`<pre>`, `<blockquote>`). This knowledge has no place in the core.","callouts":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"Evidence","level":2,"children":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"1A. `DELIMITER_CHAR_TO_SEMANTIC` constant","level":3,"children":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb:134-141"},{"type":"TextContent","text":":"}],"content":"`lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb:134-141`:","callouts":[]},{"type":"SourceBlock","children":[],"content":"DELIMITER_CHAR_TO_SEMANTIC = {\n  '-' => :source_code,\n  '=' => :example,\n  '_' => :quote,\n  '*' => :sidebar,\n  '.' => :literal,\n  '+' => :pass\n}.freeze","language":"ruby","callouts":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"1B. `resolve_semantic_from_delimiter` method","level":3,"children":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb:125-131"},{"type":"TextContent","text":":"}],"content":"`lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb:125-131`:","callouts":[]},{"type":"SourceBlock","children":[],"content":"def resolve_semantic_from_delimiter\n  delim = delimiter_type\n  return nil unless delim && delim.length >= 4\n  char = delim[0]\n  DELIMITER_CHAR_TO_SEMANTIC[char] || nil\nend","language":"ruby","callouts":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"TextContent","text":"The assumption that delimiters are ≥4 chars and the first char determines the type is an AsciiDoc parsing rule."}],"content":"The assumption that delimiters are ≥4 chars and the first char determines the type is an AsciiDoc parsing rule.","callouts":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"1C. `delimiter_to_semantic_type` in BlockBuilder — DUPLICATE of 1A","level":3,"children":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"lib/ceradoc/core_model/builder/block_builder.rb:45-58"},{"type":"TextContent","text":":"}],"content":"`lib/ceradoc/core_model/builder/block_builder.rb:45-58`:","callouts":[]},{"type":"SourceBlock","children":[],"content":"def delimiter_to_semantic_type(delimiter)\n  return nil unless delimiter && !delimiter.empty?\n  char = delimiter[0]\n  case char\n  when '-' then :source_code\n  when '=' then :example\n  when '_' then :quote\n  when '*' then :sidebar\n  when '.' then :literal\n  when '+' then :pass\n  else nil\n  end\nend","language":"ruby","callouts":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"TextContent","text":"Same mapping, different implementation — duplicated within CoreModel itself."}],"content":"Same mapping, different implementation — duplicated within CoreModel itself.","callouts":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"1D. `delimiter_type` attribute — DEPRECATED but still used","level":3,"children":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb:90-93"},{"type":"TextContent","text":":"}],"content":"`lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb:90-93`:","callouts":[]},{"type":"SourceBlock","children":[],"content":"# DEPRECATED — use block_semantic_type. Retained for backward compatibility.\nattribute :delimiter_type, :string","language":"ruby","callouts":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"TextContent","text":"Still read by "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"resolve_semantic_from_delimiter"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" at line 126."}],"content":"Still read by `resolve_semantic_from_delimiter` at line 126.","callouts":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"1E. `delimiter_length` attribute — AsciiDoc convention","level":3,"children":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb:95-97"},{"type":"TextContent","text":":"}],"content":"`lib/ceradoc/core_model/block.rb:95-97`:","callouts":[]},{"type":"SourceBlock","children":[],"content":"attribute :delimiter_length, :integer, default: -> { 4 }","language":"ruby","callouts":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"TextContent","text":"\"Number of delimiter characters\" defaulting to 4 is the AsciiDoc convention."}],"content":"\"Number of delimiter characters\" defaulting to 4 is the AsciiDoc convention.","callouts":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"1F. BlockBuilder sets `delimiter_length`","level":3,"children":[]},{"type":"ParagraphBlock","children":[{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"lib/ceradoc/core_model/builder/block_builder.rb:20,35"},{"type":"TextContent","text":":"}],"content":"`lib/ceradoc/core_model/builder/block_builder.rb:20,35`:","callouts":[]},{"type":"SourceBlock","children":[],"content":"delimiter_length: ast[:delimiter]&.to_s&.length || 4,","language":"ruby","callouts":[]},{"type":"SectionElement","title":"Fix","level":2,"children":[]},{"type":"ListBlock","marker_type":"ordered","items":[{"type":"ListItem","children":[{"type":"TextContent","text":"Remove "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"DELIMITER_CHAR_TO_SEMANTIC"},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"resolve_semantic_from_delimiter"},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"delimiter_type"},{"type":"TextContent","text":", "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"delimiter_length"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" from "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"CoreModel::Block"},{"type":"TextContent","text":"."}],"marker":"1.","content":"Remove `DELIMITER_CHAR_TO_SEMANTIC`, `resolve_semantic_from_delimiter`, `delimiter_type`, `delimiter_length` from `CoreModel::Block`."},{"type":"ListItem","children":[{"type":"TextContent","text":"Remove "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"delimiter_to_semantic_type"},{"type":"TextContent","text":" from "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"BlockBuilder"},{"type":"TextContent","text":"."}],"marker":"1.","content":"Remove `delimiter_to_semantic_type` from `BlockBuilder`."},{"type":"ListItem","children":[{"type":"TextContent","text":"Move all delimiter-to-semantics mapping to "},{"type":"MonospaceElement","children":[],"content":"ceradoc-adoc"},{"type":"TextContent","text":"'s ToCoreModel transformer, which should resolve the semantic type before constructing CoreModel objects."}],"marker":"1.","content":"Move all delimiter-to-semantics mapping to `ceradoc-a